From 02465f0885d95c415d4292cd49c56727ea7a5d33 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dominick Morales <dmorales2024@my.fit.edu>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 13:00:19 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] KVM: introspection: uapi and host interfaces

Wire format of the KVM-VMI kvmi-v7 protocol as spoken by libkvmi 1.1
(KVMI_VERSION 1, v6-compatible message ids, KVMI_EVENT_CPUID) plus the
KVM_INTROSPECTION_* VM ioctls at 0xfa-0xff and KVM_CAP_INTROSPECTION.

Per-vCPU interception state lives in struct kvm_vcpu_arch so vendor code
can merge it with KVM's own needs. EPT views, #VE, SPP and remote
mapping from kvmi-v7 are not carried over.

Based on the Bitdefender KVMI patches (kvmi-v7, kvmi-v12).

